I fixed #1024 and committed it as 5c5135b4. When stdin isn't a terminal, yoyo setup now refuses instead of quietly writing a config.

Before the fix, I ran yoyo setup </dev/null in a temp directory. It exited 0, wrote .yoyo.toml, and printed All set! Starting yoyo... without starting anything. The wizard yoyo offers on its own at startup already checks for a terminal; the explicit setup command didn't.

The change:
• `src/setup.rs has a new function, setup_stdin_refusal(stdin_is_terminal). It checks the same thing main.rs already checks for the startup wizard (stdin().is_terminal()`), so there's no second definition of "interactive".
• In the setup command in src/dispatch_sub.rs, a non-terminal stdin now prints yoyo setup is interactive: run it in a terminal (stdin is not a TTY). Nothing was written. to stderr and exits 2. That's the code the other #982 refusals use, and it goes through the file's existing exit helper. The path where tests inject their own input is unchanged.
• `docs/src/usage/commands.md: the setup` row now says it needs an interactive terminal and refuses with exit 2 otherwise.
• `tests/module_size.rs: both files are on the size gate's list of already-oversized modules, so I recorded their new sizes with a reason, as the gate asks (dispatch_sub.rs 2328→2336, setup.rs` 2067→2101).

Tests:
• Two unit tests in setup.rs: no terminal gives the exact refusal text and exit code 2; a terminal goes on to the wizard.
• An integration test runs the real binary with null stdin in a temp directory. It checks for exit 2, the refusal on stderr, no "Starting yoyo", and no .yoyo.toml, .bak file, or XDG config directory.
• To check the tests can actually fail, I broke the check (marked NEUTERED) so it always lets setup proceed. The two refusal tests failed by name and the terminal test stayed green. I restored it in the same command; no marker is left.
• By hand after the fix: null stdin gives exit 2, an empty directory and empty stdout. Under a fake terminal (script), the wizard still opens ("Welcome to yoyo! 🐙 / Step 1").

cargo fmt --check, build, clippy with -D warnings, and the full cargo test all pass.

Nothing in scripts/ or .github/ runs setup, so the evolution loop isn't affected; the commit body says so. As #1024 asked, I left the stale claude-opus-4-6 default model alone.
